{
  "schema": "narrative.intro_lines/1",
  "_about": "PARKED DRAFT (docs/narrative/pending/). Dynamic introduction lines (docs/narrative/intro-lines.md), keyed by phase, speaker, matchup, place, time of day and history. A line is picked by how many of its keys the match satisfies (the most specific wins), with no repeat inside the last ten intros. 'dummy' is the training dummy (the reference fighter), who does not speak. Every line passes the lint; unsearched by Legal; for Orb's marks.",
  "keys": {
    "phase": "touchdown (the speaker lands) | first_sight (each sees the other) | staredown (a call and an answer, left fighter first)",
    "who": "protagonist | rival",
    "vs": "rival | protagonist | dummy",
    "place": "city | town | ice | ocean | desert | mountains",
    "tod": "dawn | day | dusk | night",
    "history": "first | rematch | after_loss (the speaker lost last time) | after_win (the speaker won last time) | flattened_city (a city was flattened last stage)",
    "pair": "staredown lines with the same pair id are said together: the first, then the answer"
  },
  "lines": [
